reading: b*-1 = arithmetic cushion. If bounded below uniformly (band-flat, >0), primes have
uniform stiffness = quantitative RH-robustness on this front. If ->0 with band, the corner is
marginal everywhere (no cushion, §335 'arithmetic only tested at criticality' made quantitative).
n* being the cheapest to flip = the resonant prime is the RH-critical arithmetic dof.
